                <p><strong>IT Act 2000 S.3:</strong> Digital signature via asymmetric PKI cryptography. Legal recognition for electronic records.</p><p><strong>IT Act 2000 S.5:</strong> DSC = same legal weight as handwritten signature. Admissible under Indian Evidence Act 1872.</p><p><strong>IT Act 2000 S.35:</strong> CCA-licensed CAs authorised to issue DSCs.</p><p><strong>IT Act 2000 S.71:</strong> Misrepresentation for DSC: up to 2 years imprisonment + Rs 1L fine.</p><p><strong>CCA Jan 2021:</strong> Class 1 & 2 discontinued. Only Class 3 issued. CCA March 2023: FIPS 140-3 USB tokens mandatory.</p>

